<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Reckon Research | Adaptive placement infrastructure for AI inference</title>
<meta name="description" content="The served token: one output token delivered inside its SLO and above its quality floor. We define the unit, publish the instrument, and build the API and agents that act on it.">
<link rel="canonical" href="https://reckonresearch.com/">

<meta property="og:title" content="Adaptive placement infrastructure for AI inference">
<meta property="og:description" content="AI is the first trillion-dollar infrastructure that cannot yet state, in a standard unit, what its output costs.">
<meta property="og:url" content="https://reckonresearch.com/">
<meta property="og:type" content="website">
<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">

<style>
/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Reckon Research

   Type: Inter for prose, a monospace for every quantity. The mono is not
   decoration. This is a measurement company, and a number set in the same face
   as the sentence around it reads as prose. Set in mono it reads as a reading
   off an instrument, which is what it is.

   Colour: the navy is the mark. One accent, a signal amber, used only where
   something has actually been measured. It appears four times on the page and
   never as decoration.
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
:root{
  --ink:#0B0F1A;
  --navy:#102147;
  --slate:#5A6478;
  --hair:#E2E5EB;
  --paper:#FCFCFB;
  --amber:#B4740B;

  --sans:"Inter",-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"Segoe UI",Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;
  --mono:"SF Mono",SFMono-Regular,ui-monospace,"JetBrains Mono","Roboto Mono",Menlo,monospace;

  --gut:clamp(1.5rem,5vw,6rem);
  --rule:1px solid var(--hair);
}
*{box-sizing:border-box;margin:0;padding:0}
html{-webkit-text-size-adjust:100%}
body{
  font-family:var(--sans);
  background:var(--paper);
  color:var(--ink);
  font-size:17px;
  line-height:1.55;
  -webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;
  font-feature-settings:"ss01","cv05";
}
.wrap{max-width:1180px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 var(--gut)}
a{color:inherit}

/* --- nav ---------------------------------------------------------------- */
.nav{
  position:sticky;top:0;z-index:50;
  background:rgba(252,252,251,.88);
  backdrop-filter:saturate(180%) blur(12px);
  border-bottom:var(--rule);
}
.nav .wrap{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:2rem;height:64px}
.brand{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.55rem;text-decoration:none;flex:none}
.brand svg{display:block}
.brand span{font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.015em;font-size:1.02rem}
.nav ul{list-style:none;display:flex;gap:1.75rem;margin-left:auto;align-items:center}
.nav a.link{
  text-decoration:none;font-size:.9rem;color:var(--slate);
  padding:.25rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid transparent;transition:color .15s,border-color .15s;
}
.nav a.link:hover,.nav a.link:focus-visible{color:var(--ink);border-color:var(--ink)}
.navtoggle{display:none;margin-left:auto;background:none;border:var(--rule);border-radius:4px;
  padding:.4rem .6rem;font:inherit;font-size:.85rem;cursor:pointer;color:var(--slate)}

/* --- the measure: the page's one signature device ------------------------
   Two prices for the same model, drawn to scale. The gap is the product.
   It is the only graphic on the page and it is made of the finding itself. */
.hero{padding:clamp(3rem,6.5vw,5.5rem) 0 clamp(3rem,6vw,5rem)}
.hero .wrap{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.05fr) minmax(0,.95fr);
  gap:clamp(2rem,6vw,5rem);align-items:center}
.proof{
  font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.01em;
  color:var(--amber);margin-bottom:1.4rem;
}
h1{
  font-size:clamp(2.15rem,4.3vw,3.4rem);
  line-height:1.06;letter-spacing:-.03em;font-weight:600;
  text-wrap:balance;
}
.sub{
  margin-top:1.3rem;font-size:clamp(1.08rem,1.75vw,1.32rem);
  line-height:1.42;color:var(--slate);max-width:36ch;letter-spacing:-.012em;
}
.cta{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.75rem;margin-top:2.5rem;align-items:center}
.btn{
  display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:.4rem;
  background:var(--navy);color:#fff;text-decoration:none;
  padding:.72rem 1.15rem;border-radius:3px;font-size:.94rem;font-weight:500;
  transition:background .15s;
}
.btn:hover,.btn:focus-visible{background:#1a3468}
.install{
  font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.88rem;color:var(--slate);
  border:var(--rule);border-radius:3px;padding:.72rem 1.05rem;background:#fff;
}

.measure{border:var(--rule);border-radius:4px;background:#fff;padding:1.6rem 1.75rem}
.measure-head{
  font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.75rem;letter-spacing:0;
  color:var(--slate);margin-bottom:1.5rem;line-height:1.5;
}
.bars{display:grid;gap:.85rem}
.bar{display:grid;grid-template-columns:5.5rem minmax(0,1fr) auto;align-items:center;gap:.85rem}
.bar-name{font-size:.88rem;color:var(--slate)}
.bar-track{height:22px;position:relative;background:#F4F5F8;border-radius:2px}
.bar-fill{height:100%;background:var(--navy);opacity:.9;border-radius:2px;min-width:3px}
.bar.hi .bar-fill{background:var(--amber);opacity:.9}
.bar-val{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.92rem;color:var(--ink);white-space:nowrap}
.bar.hi .bar-val{color:var(--amber)}
.measure-note{margin-top:1.1rem;font-size:.87rem;color:var(--slate);max-width:56ch}

/* --- sections ----------------------------------------------------------- */
section.blk{border-top:var(--rule);padding:clamp(3rem,6.5vw,5.5rem) 0}
.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:7rem minmax(0,1fr);gap:clamp(1rem,4vw,3.5rem)}
.num{
  font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.82rem;color:var(--navy);
  letter-spacing:.02em;padding-top:.4rem;font-weight:500;
}
.body{max-width:60ch}
h2{
  font-size:clamp(1.55rem,2.9vw,2.15rem);line-height:1.14;
  letter-spacing:-.025em;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:1.35rem;text-wrap:balance;
}
.lede{font-size:clamp(1.15rem,2.1vw,1.42rem);line-height:1.42;letter-spacing:-.014em;margin-bottom:1.35rem}
.body p{margin-bottom:1.05rem;color:var(--slate)}
.body p.ink{color:var(--ink)}
.body strong{color:var(--ink);font-weight:600}
.pull{
  border-left:2px solid var(--navy);padding-left:1.15rem;margin:1.6rem 0;
  font-size:1.06rem;color:var(--ink);
}
.links{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:1.5rem;margin-top:1.7rem}
.links a{
  text-decoration:none;font-size:.93rem;color:var(--navy);font-weight:500;
  border-bottom:1px solid rgba(16,33,71,.25);padding-bottom:1px;transition:border-color .15s;
}
.links a:hover,.links a:focus-visible{border-color:var(--navy)}

/* --- the unit, set as a definition -------------------------------------- */
.defn{border:var(--rule);border-radius:4px;background:#fff;padding:1.6rem 1.75rem;margin-bottom:1.6rem}
.defn .term{font-size:1.28rem;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.02em}
.defn .abbr{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.9rem;color:var(--amber);margin-left:.6rem}
.defn .gloss{margin-top:.6rem;color:var(--ink);font-size:1.02rem;line-height:1.5}
.defn .unit{
  margin-top:1rem;padding-top:.9rem;border-top:var(--rule);
  font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.85rem;color:var(--slate);
}

.drops{list-style:none;margin:1.4rem 0;border-top:var(--rule)}
.drops li{
  display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(9rem,14rem) minmax(0,1fr);
  gap:1rem;padding:.72rem 0;border-bottom:var(--rule);font-size:.95rem;align-items:baseline;
}
.drops .m{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.86rem;color:var(--ink)}
.drops .d{color:var(--slate)}

/* --- three tools -------------------------------------------------------- */
.tools{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:1px;background:var(--hair);
  border:var(--rule);border-radius:4px;overflow:hidden;margin-top:.4rem}
.tool{background:#fff;padding:1.5rem;display:flex;flex-direction:column}
.tool h3{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:1rem;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.55rem;letter-spacing:-.01em}
.tool p{font-size:.93rem;color:var(--slate);margin:0}
pre{
  font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.88rem;background:var(--ink);color:#E8EAF0;
  padding:.95rem 1.15rem;border-radius:3px;margin-top:1.4rem;overflow-x:auto;
}
pre .p{color:#8FA0C4}

/* --- working with us ---------------------------------------------------- */
.ways{list-style:none;margin-top:.4rem}
.ways li{padding:1.15rem 0;border-bottom:var(--rule)}
.ways li:first-child{border-top:var(--rule)}
.ways b{display:block;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.25rem}
.ways span{color:var(--slate);font-size:.96rem}

footer{border-top:var(--rule);padding:2.5rem 0 3.5rem;font-size:.88rem;color:var(--slate)}
footer .row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:1.5rem;align-items:center}
footer a{text-decoration:none;border-bottom:1px solid var(--hair)}
footer a:hover{border-color:var(--slate)}
footer .rt{margin-left:auto}

@media (max-width:820px){
  .nav ul{
    display:none;position:absolute;top:64px;left:0;right:0;background:var(--paper);
    border-bottom:var(--rule);flex-direction:column;gap:0;padding:.5rem var(--gut) 1rem;
  }
  .nav ul.open{display:flex}
  .nav ul li{width:100%;border-top:var(--rule)}
  .nav a.link{display:block;padding:.85rem 0;font-size:1rem}
  .navtoggle{display:block}
  .grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:.6rem}
  .num{padding-top:0}
  .tools{grid-template-columns:1fr}
  .drops li{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:.15rem}
  .bar{grid-template-columns:5rem minmax(0,1fr) auto;gap:.6rem}
  .hero .wrap{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:2.5rem}
  .measure{padding:1.25rem}

}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){*{animation:none!important;transition:none!important}}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<nav class="nav">
  <div class="wrap">
    <a class="brand" href="/">
      <svg width="20" height="24" viewBox="0 0 20 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M10 1.5l1.6 2.2H8.4L10 1.5zM7.2 4.6h5.6v1.5H7.2V4.6zM8 6.9h4l.7 8.4H7.3L8 6.9z" fill="#102147"/>
        <path d="M10 12.4v9.8m0 0c-2.6 0-4.6-1.9-4.9-4.3m4.9 4.3c2.6 0 4.6-1.9 4.9-4.3M6.6 14.9H13.4" stroke="#102147" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/>
      </svg>
      <span>Reckon Research</span>
    </a>
    <button class="navtoggle" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="navmenu">Menu</button>
    <ul id="navmenu">
      <li><a class="link" href="/infrastructure/">Infrastructure</a></li>
      <li><a class="link" href="/index/">The Index</a></li>
      <li><a class="link" href="/research/">Research</a></li>
      <li><a class="link" href="https://docs.reckonresearch.com">Docs</a></li>
      <li><a class="link" href="/contact/">Contact</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</nav>

<header class="hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div>
    <p class="proof">The same model can cost 40x more in one placement than another</p>
    <h1>Adaptive placement infrastructure for AI inference</h1>
    <p class="sub">To measure what compute produces, and move every workload to where it produces most.</p>
    <div class="cta">
      <a class="btn" href="https://themissingmeter.org">Read the paper &rarr;</a>
      <code class="install">pip install berth-placement</code>
    </div>
    </div>

    <!-- The signature. Two production services, same weights, same hardware,
         same target met. Drawn to scale so the gap is the point rather than
         the numbers. This is the finding, not an illustration of it. -->
    <div class="measure">
      <p class="measure-head">Two production services &middot; identical weights &middot; identical hardware &middot; same target met</p>
      <div class="bars">
        <div class="bar">
          <span class="bar-name">Service A</span>
          <div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" style="width:2.5%"></div></div>
          <span class="bar-val">$1.06</span>
        </div>
        <div class="bar hi">
          <span class="bar-name">Service B</span>
          <div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" style="width:100%"></div></div>
          <span class="bar-val">$41.86</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="measure-note">Cost per million served tokens. Nobody chose this. Neither team could see it.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="blk">
  <div class="wrap grid">
    <div class="num">1.0</div>
    <div class="body">
      <p class="lede ink"><strong>AI is the first trillion-dollar infrastructure that cannot yet state, in a standard unit, what its output costs.</strong></p>
      <p>That spending buys hours. What anyone actually needs is work delivered before a deadline. No standard unit connects the two, so nobody can say what a workload costs, compare two places to run it, or prove a change made anything better.</p>
      <p class="ink">Every efficiency gain in AI today is unmeasurable. It is why capital cannot tell a good decision from a lucky one, and why the same model can cost 40x more in one placement than another while meeting the same target.</p>
      <p class="ink"><strong>We built the missing meter, and the system that acts on what it reads.</strong></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <div class="wrap grid">
    <div class="num">2.0</div>
    <div class="body">
      <h2>The unit</h2>
      <div class="defn">
        <div><span class="term">The served token</span><span class="abbr">SVT</span></div>
        <p class="gloss">One output token delivered inside its service-level objective and above its quality floor.</p>
        <p class="unit">price notation &nbsp;$/MSVT&nbsp; &middot; &nbsp;dollars per million served tokens</p>
      </div>
      <p class="ink">A token that arrives after its deadline is not a cheap token. It is not a token.</p>
      <p>Every existing measure drops something.</p>
      <ul class="drops">
        <li><span class="m">$ / GPU-hour</span><span class="d">drops the output</span></li>
        <li><span class="m">$ / raw token</span><span class="d">drops the deadline and the quality</span></li>
        <li><span class="m">benchmarks</span><span class="d">drop the price</span></li>
        <li><span class="m">uptime SLAs</span><span class="d">drop everything but the deadline</span></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="ink">The served token is the first measure of AI compute that carries all of it at once: the work, the deadline, the quality, and the invoice.</p>
      <div class="pull">The specification is published, and anyone may use it, including the people who compete with us. <strong>A unit nobody else may use is not a unit.</strong></div>
      <div class="links">
        <a href="https://themissingmeter.org">The Missing Meter</a>
        <a href="https://docs.reckonresearch.com/the-unit/">The specification</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <div class="wrap grid">
    <div class="num">3.0</div>
    <div class="body">
      <h2>Adaptive placement</h2>
      <p class="lede ink">Deciding which chip, which provider, and at which price a model should run under a stated p99, then moving it as prices, capacity, and traffic shift.</p>
      <p><strong>The problem:</strong> that answer changes. A model version ships. A price moves. Traffic shifts. Most teams decide once and never check.</p>
      <p class="ink"><strong>What makes it adaptive:</strong> it never stops deciding. Prices move, models ship, capacity changes. So does the right placement.</p>
      <div class="links">
        <a href="/infrastructure/">How it works</a>
        <a href="https://docs.reckonresearch.com/quickstart/">Run it yourself</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <div class="wrap grid">
    <div class="num">4.0</div>
    <div class="body">
      <h2>The infrastructure</h2>
      <p>Three pieces. The unit is measured, the measurement is checked, and the decision is acted on.</p>
      <div class="tools">
        <div class="tool">
          <h3>berth</h3>
          <p>Predicts what a workload costs and how fast it runs on a given accelerator, before you rent it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tool">
          <h3>sounding</h3>
          <p>Measures the real thing and checks the prediction.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tool">
          <h3>pilot</h3>
          <p>Watches for change, adapts the placement, and proves what the change saved.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <pre><span class="p">$</span> pip install berth-placement</pre>
      <p style="margin-top:1.2rem">All open source. All reproducible from published traces.</p>
      <div class="links"><a href="/infrastructure/">Infrastructure</a></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <div class="wrap grid">
    <div class="num">5.0</div>
    <div class="body">
      <h2>It is arithmetic</h2>
      <p class="ink">The model is a page of physics: bytes moved, work done, time under load. No learned components and no training data, so every number is auditable by hand.</p>
      <p>That matters because an answer is only worth having if you can check it. Every prediction ships with the term that produced it and a label saying whether that term rests on a measurement or a specification sheet.</p>
      <p>Where the physics stops describing the machine, we will learn the difference. Knowing exactly where it stops is what makes that possible, and mapping that boundary is the research.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <div class="wrap grid">
    <div class="num">6.0</div>
    <div class="body">
      <h2>Measured, and published either way</h2>
      <p class="ink">An untuned model, fitted on one accelerator, predicts hardware it has never seen to within ten percent. The bar was set and published before the first measurement was taken.</p>
      <p>Every trace is downloadable. Every number is reproducible. When the instrument itself is wrong, we publish that too, with the mechanism and the test that catches it if it returns.</p>
      <div class="pull"><strong>A measurement tool that has never been caught lying has not been used hard enough.</strong></div>
      <div class="links">
        <a href="/index/">The Placement Index</a>
        <a href="/validation/">Validation</a>
        <a href="/research/">How we work</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <div class="wrap grid">
    <div class="num">7.0</div>
    <div class="body">
      <h2>Working with us</h2>
      <ul class="ways">
        <li><b>If you serve your own models</b><span>Use berth and tell us where its numbers are wrong. Bring traces.</span></li>
        <li><b>If you operate hardware or a cloud</b><span>Contribute measurement access under our published governance.</span></li>
        <li><b>If you work on performance modelling, systems learning, or market design</b><span>This is a genuine open problem with a deterministic verifier and a live environment attached.</span></li>
      </ul>
      <div class="links"><a href="mailto:hello@reckonresearch.com">hello@reckonresearch.com</a></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<footer>
  <div class="wrap row">
    <span>Reckon Research</span>
    <a href="/infrastructure/">Infrastructure</a>
    <a href="/index/">The Index</a>
    <a href="/research/">Research</a>
    <a href="https://docs.reckonresearch.com">Docs</a>
    <a href="https://github.com/reckonresearch/berth">GitHub</a>
    <span class="rt">Apache-2.0 &middot; specification CC BY 4.0</span>
  </div>
</footer>

<script>
  var t = document.querySelector('.navtoggle'), m = document.getElementById('navmenu');
  t.addEventListener('click', function () {
    var open = m.classList.toggle('open');
    t.setAttribute('aria-expanded', open);
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
